# Font Guidelines

## Web Safe Font Requirements

- **ONLY use web-safe fonts** that are pre-installed on the majority of operating systems
- **NO external font libraries** (Google Fonts, Adobe Fonts, etc.)
- **NO custom font hosting** that requires HTTP requests
- Always implement **font stacks** with 3-5 fallback options that visually resemble each other
- Ensure fonts display consistently across Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, and Android

## ⚠️ ANDROID IS THE MOST RESTRICTIVE PLATFORM

**Android has the smallest pre-installed font library of any major operating system.**

### Android Default Fonts (ALL Versions)
According to [exeideas.com](https://www.exeideas.com/2016/02/list-of-default-fonts-in-android.html):

**There are only THREE fonts pre-installed on Android:**
1. **Normal (Droid Sans)** - Sans-serif
   - Regular, Italic, Bold, Bold-italic
2. **Serif (Droid Serif)** - Serif
   - Regular, Italic, Bold, Bold-italic  
3. **Monospace (Droid Sans Mono)** - Monospace
   - Regular only

### Android 4.0+ (Roboto Era)
Additional fonts available:
- Roboto (regular, italic, bold, bold-italic)
- Roboto Light (light, light-italic)
- Roboto Thin (thin, thin-italic)
- Roboto Condensed (regular, italic, bold, bold-italic)
- Noto Serif

### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Android Monospace Is NOT Truly Monospace!

According to [Stack Overflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/42557853/android-monospace-space-nbsp-width-is-different-than-character-width):

**The space character (`&nbsp;` or regular space) has a DIFFERENT WIDTH than other characters in Android's monospace fonts.**

This breaks:
- ASCII art layouts
- Code formatting
- Tabular data alignment
- Box drawing characters

**Solution:** Do NOT rely on monospace for precise character alignment on Android. Use CSS Grid or tables instead.

