## Fonts to AVOID (Limited Platform Support)

### Windows-Only Fonts (NOT Web Safe)
- Calibri (83% Windows, 39% macOS)
- Segoe UI (75% Windows, 0% macOS)
- Consolas (83% Windows, 35% macOS)
- Lucida Console (99% Windows, 0% macOS)
- Cambria (83% Windows, 35% macOS)

### macOS/iOS-Only Fonts (NOT Web Safe)
- Futura (94% macOS, 1% Windows)
- Geneva (99% macOS, 2% Windows)
- Helvetica Neue (macOS/iOS, low Windows support)
- Didot (93% macOS, 0% Windows)
- Gill Sans (95% macOS, 59% Windows)

### Android-Only Fonts (NOT Web Safe)
- Roboto (unless you target Android 4.0+ specifically)
- Noto Sans/Serif
- Droid fonts (outside of Android)

## Testing Requirements

### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Test on Physical Devices

Before finalizing fonts, test on:
- [ ] **Physical Android device** (NOT just emulator) - Android is the most restrictive!
- [ ] Windows PC (Chrome, Firefox, Edge)
- [ ] macOS (Safari, Chrome, Firefox)
- [ ] iPhone/iPad (Safari, Chrome)
- [ ] Older Android device (pre-4.0 if supporting legacy)

### Specific Android Tests
- [ ] Verify monospace spacing (spaces vs characters)
- [ ] Check Roboto fallback on Android 4.0+
- [ ] Test Droid Sans fallback on older Android
- [ ] Verify serif font displays (should be Droid Serif)
- [ ] Test ASCII art or box-drawing characters (will likely break!)

### General Font Tests
- [ ] Font renders correctly at all sizes
- [ ] Line height is readable (1.5-1.75 for body)
- [ ] Text remains readable at minimum 16px
- [ ] Special characters display correctly
- [ ] Font stack degrades gracefully

## Implementation Example

### HTML
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Web Safe Fonts Example</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: 16px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        
        h1, h2, h3 {
            font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
            line-height: 1.2;
        }
        
        code, pre {
            font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace;
            /* WARNING: Do NOT rely on monospace for alignment on Android! */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Web Safe Typography</h1>
    <p>This text will display consistently across all platforms.</p>
    <code>Monospace text for code examples</code>
</body>
</html>
```

## Quick Reference: Platform Priority (Most to Least Restrictive)

1. **Android** - Only 3 core fonts, test here FIRST
2. **Linux** - Variable, depends on distribution
3. **Windows** - Good coverage, some exclusive fonts
4. **iOS/macOS** - Excellent coverage, Apple-exclusive fonts

